test_kernels -- the geometry kernels against independent answers (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_kernel_tests.sh [path-to-del_vor]    about 1 s
  open summary.html

  Runs del_vor_selftest (test/del_vor_selftest.F90, built next to
  del_vor) on 2000 random triangles and 2000 random tets (fixed seed,
  the same cells on every machine), then on the three meshes of
  ../test_voronoi_gold/inputs.

WHAT IS CHECKED (tolerance 1e-10 unless stated; all relative)

  cot2d     triangles in random orientations in 3D: the kernel's
            A(ab)/d(ab) equals cot(angle opposite ab)/2
  circ3d    the tet circumcenter is equally far from the 4 vertices
  dual3d    the tet kernel's A(ab)/d(ab) equals
              (cot(t_c) h_abc + cot(t_d) h_abd) / 4
            the dual piece of edge ab being two right triangles
            (midpoint, face circumcenter, tet circumcenter); t_c the
            angle at c in face abc, h_abc the signed distance of the
            tet circumcenter from face abc. Computed from angles and
            distances, not from the kernel's cross products.
  perp3d    each Voronoi dual piece is perpendicular to its edge
  part2d    for ANY cell point (random, even outside the triangle) the
  part3d    vertex shares add up to the cell's area (volume); random
            cell and face points in 3D. Needed by the median and hybrid
            policies to come.
  shift     the same tet at the origin and at (7e5, 3.2e6, 1.5e3),
            cells of size 1: A/d agree to 1e-8 (the coordinates'
            own rounding is 7e-10)
  closure   on each mesh: the dual-face vector areas around every
            vertex not on the mesh's bounding box add up to zero

  MEASURED
  p1_3d     the tet A/d against the P1 finite-element stiffness
            -V grad(phi_a).grad(phi_b): they are NOT equal in 3D (they
            are in 2D); shows the size of the difference
  shift_voronoi_det4x4
            the shift test with lanl/voronoi's 4x4-determinant
            circumcenter: it loses every digit at these coordinates

PICTURES (logs/)

  cot2d.svg     an obtuse sample triangle, its dual pieces, kernel
                against cot/2 for each edge
  dual3d.svg    a sample tet and the 6 dual pieces; kernel against the
                right-triangle formula (and the P1 stiffness)
  shift.svg     the shift error, del_vor against voronoi's method
  closure.svg   mesh_3D with each inner vertex colored by the net
                vector area of its dual cell

FILES

  run_kernel_tests.sh   runner (work/, logs/)
  check_kernels.py      reads selftest.out, pictures, summary.html
